<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ēversĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		everto, I. B.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>An overthrowing.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">columnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 1, 2, 5</span></i>
			.—In plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eversiones vehiculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					22, 17, 20, § 43</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Esp., <i>a destructive overthrow</i>, <i>subversion</i>, <i>destruction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">templorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 5, 10, 97</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					1, 12, 7</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 69</span></i>. —In
				plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eversiones urbium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					2, 16, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A turning out</i>, <i>expulsion</i>
			from one's possession: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">possidentium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					3, 13, 9</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>A turning out</i>, <i>expulsion</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matricis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 2, 1, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (acc. to I. A. 2.), <i>subversion</i>, <i>destruction</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hinc rerum publicarum eversiones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Sen. 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rei familiaris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					6, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 31, 99</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 5, 10, 28</span></i>.</div>
